silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_5__step_traceable_iff__locate_o_extract_o_key_o_cite_=_valid_natural a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, the chain protocol is traceable because every step is a natural transformation from the witness incoming profile (source file) to its outgoing profile (typed claims it supports). A chain that skips a step breaks the natural transformation. The dashed red shortcut from SourceFile to Witness (bypassing extract, key, cite) is not a natural transformation; it is a short-circuit that produces an untracked witness." .
